 518:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/tasks.c **** /* Context switches are held pending while the scheduler is suspended.  Also,
 519:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/tasks.c ****  * interrupts must not manipulate the xStateListItem of a TCB, or any of the
 520:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/tasks.c ****  * lists the xStateListItem can be referenced from, if the scheduler is suspended.
 521:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/tasks.c ****  * If an interrupt needs to unblock a task while the scheduler is suspended then it
 522:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/tasks.c ****  * moves the task's event list item into the xPendingReadyList, ready for the
 523:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/tasks.c ****  * kernel to move the task from the pending ready list into the real ready list
 524:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/tasks.c ****  * when the scheduler is unsuspended.  The pending ready list itself can only be
 525:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/tasks.c ****  * accessed from a critical section.
 526:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/tasks.c ****  *
